{
  "name": "swordfish",
  "_about": "SCULPTED (2026-11-05, docs/engines.md 'the sculpt overlay'): a swordfish, 3.1 m with its sword -- the BILL long, flat and broad (a third of its length, a low ridge down its middle) over a short pointed lower jaw, a big eye; a robust round-bodied torpedo, deepest a third back, to a slim peduncle with one big keel each side; the tall rigid SICKLE first dorsal on a short base just behind the head, the tiny second dorsal and second anal by the tail, the first anal's smaller sickle, long sickle pectorals set low, NO pelvic fins, and the great LUNATE tail (the fins thin plates, details beside the field, their outlines rounded, faint rays fanning from each root and the membrane paler toward its edge: the coat pattern `finrays`, coatpat.js 33); dark bronze-purple above shading to a pale silvery brown below (`shade`). A SWIMMER (the fish's plumbing: `fly`, `alt` its depth; not put in the lake -- a fish of the open ocean). Its spine is four bones a beat apart (body, mid, stock, tail): the tail beats, the body stays stiff (thunniform). SHARP PASS 2 (2026-11-08): the pointed parts -- bill (1 in all) -- are the engine's sharp `horn`s (sharp.js), made from the field shapes they replaced by tools/creaturegen/sharp/ (claws.py, teeth.py, spikes.py, antlers.py, bills.py): rooted in the body, tips pointed; RE-RUN those after this species' generator.",
